      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reraising this from the first round, I do not think it landed on the change. Neither handler table covers GICR_SETLPIR (0x40) or GICR_CLRLPIR (0x48), so an access to either falls through handle_emulation to pkvm_handle_forward_req and reaches the physical register. Forcing has_direct_lpi off in the driver does not bind a host that is not cooperating.\n\nPhysical LPIs target the host rather than a protected VM, so this is the host injecting into itself, which is why I did not push before. It is a two line fix next to INVLPIR and INVALLR, could we trap and reject them the same way?\n\nMore generally, the fall-through forwards anything not in the table, and RD_base has IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED regions. Should the default be deny?",
