      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Physical LPIs target the host rather than a protected VM, so this is the host injecting into itself, which is why I did not push before. It is a two line fix next to INVLPIR and INVALLR, could we trap and reject them the same way?\n\nAdded RAZ_WI handlers for GICR_SETLPIR (0x40) and GICR_CLRLPIR (0x48) to both `redist_handlers` and `redist_handlers_pre_init`. Accesses to these registers are now trapped instead of falling through to physical HW.\n\n\u003e More generally, the fall-through forwards anything not in the table, and RD_base has IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED regions. Should the default be deny?\n\nI don\u0027t think that is a feasible solution. Each vendor could have a different set of registers in those regions and we could break their functionality.",
